   "platform": "x",
   "title": "NNPC Weekly Highlights for October 11 to 16, 2026, was packed with major milestones for NNPC Limited, from strong financial performance to g",
   "url": "https://x.com/EleluAyoola/status/2111404247736598547",
   "snippet": "NNPC Weekly Highlights for October 11 to 16, 2026, was packed with major milestones for NNPC Limited, from strong financial performance to global transparency recognition and customer-focused innovations.\n\nKicking off the week on October 11, NNPC Limited announced the extension of its popular N66 discount promo until 31st October 2026. Based on popular demand, the promo now covers both PMS and AGO, giving customers more opportunity to save at NNPC Retail stations nationwide.\n\nOn October 12, Group Chief Executive Officer, Engr. Bashir Bayo Ojulari, presented the Company's 2025 Audited Financial Statement to President Bola Ahmed Tinubu at the Presidential Villa, Abuja. The statement highlighted N7.2 trillion Profit After Tax, N8.8 trillion dividend and N34.5 trillion revenue, underscoring NNPC's strong financial health and value to the Federation.\n\nOn the same day, the Company released its Monthly Report Summary for August 2026, reporting strong performance. Crude Oil and Condensate Production stood at 1.69 mmbopd, Natural Gas Production at 7,680 mmscf/d, Revenue at N3.737 trillion, Profit After Tax at N431 billion, and Statutory Payments at N9.487 trillion. Upstream Pipeline Availability was 100 percent, OB3 Completion at 100 percent, and AKK Completion at 95 percent. The report also noted that Profit Tax surged by 54.6 percent to N631 billion, with cumulative revenue rising to N7.4 trillion and statutory payments reaching N49 trillion for January to August.\n\nAlso on October 12, NNPC announced it will host the 2026 Contractors and Partners CEO HSE Conference on 21st and 22nd October 2026 in Abuja. Themed Strengthening HSE Excellence Through Partnership and Operational Excellence, the conference will hold at the TY Danjuma Foundation. On October 15, the Company confirmed that GCEO Engr. Bashir Bayo Ojulari will deliver the keynote address.\n\nAt the 2026 EITI Global Conference in Brussels, NNPC reaffirmed its commitment to openness. On October 14, Head of Global Compliance, Murjanatu Gamawa, reaffirmed the Company's commitment to full disclosure and accountable governance. On October 16, that commitment received global validation when Mark Robinson, Executive Director of the Extractive Industries Transparency Initiative, received NNPC Ltd's 2025 Audited Financial Statement on the sidelines of the conference and lauded the Company's progress on transparency.",
   "body": "NNPC Weekly Highlights for October 11 to 16, 2026, was packed with major milestones for NNPC Limited, from strong financial performance to global transparency recognition and customer-focused innovations.\n\nKicking off the week on October 11, NNPC Limited announced the extension of its popular N66 discount promo until 31st October 2026. Based on popular demand, the promo now covers both PMS and AGO, giving customers more opportunity to save at NNPC Retail stations nationwide.\n\nOn October 12, Group Chief Executive Officer, Engr. Bashir Bayo Ojulari, presented the Company's 2025 Audited Financial Statement to President Bola Ahmed Tinubu at the Presidential Villa, Abuja. The statement highlighted N7.2 trillion Profit After Tax, N8.8 trillion dividend and N34.5 trillion revenue, underscoring NNPC's strong financial health and value to the Federation.\n\nOn the same day, the Company released its Monthly Report Summary for August 2026, reporting strong performance. Crude Oil and Condensate Production stood at 1.69 mmbopd, Natural Gas Production at 7,680 mmscf/d, Revenue at N3.737 trillion, Profit After Tax at N431 billion, and Statutory Payments at N9.487 trillion. Upstream Pipeline Availability was 100 percent, OB3 Completion at 100 percent, and AKK Completion at 95 percent. The report also noted that Profit Tax surged by 54.6 percent to N631 billion, with cumulative revenue rising to N7.4 trillion and statutory payments reaching N49 trillion for January to August.\n\nAlso on October 12, NNPC announced it will host the 2026 Contractors and Partners CEO HSE Conference on 21st and 22nd October 2026 in Abuja. Themed Strengthening HSE Excellence Through Partnership and Operational Excellence, the conference will hold at the TY Danjuma Foundation. On October 15, the Company confirmed that GCEO Engr. Bashir Bayo Ojulari will deliver the keynote address.\n\nAt the 2026 EITI Global Conference in Brussels, NNPC reaffirmed its commitment to openness. On October 14, Head of Global Compliance, Murjanatu Gamawa, reaffirmed the Company's commitment to full disclosure and accountable governance. On October 16, that commitment received global validation when Mark Robinson, Executive Director of the Extractive Industries Transparency Initiative, received NNPC Ltd's 2025 Audited Financial Statement on the sidelines of the conference and lauded the Company's progress on transparency.",
